\DOC ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED

\TYPE {ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED : thm -> thm -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Completely proves a machine-code correctness goal whose byte list is described
by a bridging equation, deriving it from the corresponding theorem about the
variant program.

\DESCRIBE
{bridge_th : thm} is an equation stating that the program's byte list equals a
fixed prefix appended to the variant program's byte list at a shifted program
counter; {th : thm} is the already-proved correctness theorem for that variant
program, from which the goal is obtained. The goal's conclusion is a
correctness statement: a universally quantified implication whose conclusion is
an {ensures} triple, possibly itself under an existential quantifier binding a
function variable. The tactic discharges such a goal outright.
{
         A ?- t
     ==============  ADD_IBT_TAC_PARAMETRIZED bridge_th th
}
{
   
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this closing behaviour, on goals with no
assumptions whose conclusions are machine-code correctness specifications
matching the supplied bridging equation and source theorem.

\ENDDOC
